\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For each $n\geq 4$, does a constant C(n) exist such that every connected complete smooth boundaryless Riemannian n-manifold satisfying $\int (4|\nabla \varphi |^{2}+Scal\cdot \varphi ^{2})\geq \int \varphi ^{2}$ for every real compactly supported smooth $\varphi $ admits a continuous map into a simplicial complex of dimension $\leq n-2$, each fiber having metric diameter $\leq C(n)$?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For each $n\geq 4$, does a constant C(n) exist such that every connected complete smooth boundaryless Riemannian n-manifold satisfying $\int (4|\nabla \varphi |^{2}+Scal\cdot \varphi ^{2})\geq \int \varphi ^{2}$ for every real compactly supported smooth $\varphi $ admits a continuous map into a simplicial complex of dimension $\leq n-2$, each fiber having metric diameter $\leq C(n)$?

\subsection{Sources}
